Raj: Yes. Keep an eye on the journal and request age. Both links are in the ticket.

3
00:00:16.008 --> 00:00:25.392
Hannah: At twenty hundred I check the oldest request. Over two hours means escalation. Have I missed anything?

4
00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:31.776
Anika: The resume approval. You don't re-enable fetching just because the process has stayed up.

5
00:00:31.776 --> 00:00:39.960
Priya: Right. Just to recap, short-term stability isn't a fix. The investigation remains open.

6
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:47.040
Lukas: I take the timeline if we open an incident. Hannah keeps coordination and primary response.

7
00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:53.112
Raj: One action item before I hand over: confirm you can open the saved evidence.

8
00:00:53.112 --> 00:00:59.544
Hannah: I can. The links and restricted log access both work from my account.

9
00:00:59.544 --> 00:01:06.984
Anika: Good. And no customer-facing promise of recovery yet. We haven't resumed exports.

10
00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:13.920
Priya: Agreed, right? We'll report the current delay honestly and update after the scheduled check.

